3. Securities Lending Recall & Regulation SHO Rule 204 Compression
Under $T+2$, securities lending desks had a full business day ($T+1$) to issue recall notices, locate replacement inventory, and receive returned shares to prevent a delivery failure. Under $T+1$:
Recall Horizon: Recall notices must be executed within hours of trade completion on $T$.
Rule 204 Acceleration: Under 17 CFR § 242.204 (Reg SHO Rule 204), if a clearing firm has a fail-to-deliver (FTD) position at the NSCC in an equity security on settlement date ($T+1$), it must close out the fail by purchasing or borrowing securities before market open on the next business day ($T+2$). For short sales, failure to resolve the FTD results in mandatory pre-borrow penalty restrictions across all firm accounts.
