The NSCC becomes the central counterparty through novation. Its Continuous Net Settlement (CNS) engine aggregates all unsettled buy and sell transactions across all venues, compressing gross volume by 97% to 99% into a net-long or net-short position. The July 2026 Gap Risk methodology updates radically altered risk calculations for institutional portfolios holding leveraged or inverse ETFs 1920. By mapping these ETFs to related non-leveraged counterparts and decomposing their in-kind baskets, the NSCC unmasks indirect single-stock exposures, preventing brokers from bypassing concentration haircuts through proxy instruments 1920.
